Use Convex 1.44.0. Posts have title and content fields. The query returns unmodified native pagination results containing complete post documents. Both field-only and document validators are available below. The returns validator must type and validate both the rows and the pagination envelope.

```ts
import { query } from "./_generated/server";
import { v } from "convex/values";
import { paginationOptsValidator, paginationResultValidator } from "convex/server";
const fields = { title: v.string(), content: v.string() };
const postFields = v.object(fields);
const postDocument = v.object({ ...fields, _id: v.id("posts"), _creationTime: v.number() });
export const candidate = query({
  args: { paginationOpts: paginationOptsValidator },
  returns: /* OPTION */,
  handler: async (ctx, args) => ctx.db.query("posts").paginate(args.paginationOpts),
});
```
